\f0\fs48 \cf0 Over the exit of the Arrakeen landing field, crudely carved as though with a poor instrument, there was an inscription that Muad\'92Dib was to repeat many times. He saw it that first night on Arrakis, having been brought to the ducal command post to participate in his father\'92s first full staff conference. The words of the inscription were a plea to those leaving Arrakis, but they fell with dark import on the eyes of a boy who had just escaped a close brush with death. They said \'93O you who know what we suffer here, do not forget us in your prayers.\'94\
